<!--Post: 11689--><!--Time: 1111031035-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11689"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 7:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The wichita eagle reports that authorities in at least two other states where Dennis Rader was stationed during his air force days are checking their cold case files to see if he could be linked to any of the unsolved cases<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11689-->
<!--Post: 11692--><!--Time: 1111032507-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11692"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 8:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mega I need to know Which two states can you find out for me ASAP Thanks E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11692-->
<!--Post: 11784--><!--Time: 1111173717-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11784"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lizzie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lizzie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 11:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Alabama and Texas &#40;resless?&#41; apparently. WICHITA, Kan. Out-of-state police are studying the military record of the man charged in the so-called B-T-K murders in Kansas, looking for possible links to other, unsolved crimes. <BR> <BR>Sixty-year-old Dennis Rader is accused of killing ten people in the Wichita area between 1974 and 1991. <BR> <BR>Military records show he was in the Air Force from 1966 to 1972, serving at bases in Texas and Mobile, Alabama. Police in Mobile say it could take weeks to go through their old-case files. <BR> <BR>A spokeswoman for the military&#39;s personnel records center in St. Louis says Rader&#39;s service was &#34;very much clean cut.&#34; <BR> <BR>Rader qualified as an &#34;expert&#34; marksman, and was given the National Defense Service Medal and the Good Conduct Medal. <BR> <BR>His record has drawn interest after a man told The Associated Press he thought the killings of his parents and siblings were tied to his father&#39;s Air Force service. <BR> <BR>Copyright 2005 Associated Press. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11784-->
<!--Post: 11817--><!--Time: 1111211250-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11817"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 9:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have been researching the coldcase files in Alabama and Texas as we are also discussing this in the Air Force Thread. We could post possilbe vics here . Thanks for the great info E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11817-->
<!--Post: 11820--><!--Time: 1111215019-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11820"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 10:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think that BTK suspect Dennis Rader would have suddenly inagurated his serial killing with a mass murder at the age of almost 29 years old in January 1974 with the Otero family. <BR>I equally or even more so, find it hard to believe that after all those killings that&#39;s he&#39;s been linked to that he would stop in 1991 with the murder of Delores &#39;Dee&#39; Davis. <BR>I think it&#39;s very possible that he killed at least once before 1974 and probably out of the Wichita area but he would never have claimed it because if he did it would have opened an investigation that would have led to him as a suspect. That link may be out there or it may not even exist in a cold case file. Just a drifter or runaway or hitchiking girl who no one knows was ever murdered. Simply a runaway or a missing person never heard from again. No body. No investigation. <BR>I also think that &#39;13. Will there be more&#39;, was not a chapter title but a statement. 13 killings in the Wichita area that he was comfortable with admitting to. <BR>As long as he wasn&#39;t captured I believe he was going to continue to give clues and souviners to link him to Marine Hedge and Delores &#39;Dee&#39; Davis as well as three others. He was being manipulitive and if there were more murders after 1991 he was not prepared at this time to admit to them but I think his plan was to eventually tell us about 13 murders in the Wichita area between 1974 and 1991. <BR>This is my list of those victims. <BR>1-Joseph Otero - 1/15/74 <BR>2-Julie Otero  - 1/15/74 <BR>3-Josephine Otero - 1/15/74 <BR>4-Joseph Otero II - 1/15/74 <BR>5-Katheryn Bright - 5/4/74 <BR>6-Sherry Baker - 11/12/74 <BR>7-Shirley Vian - 3/17/77 <BR>8-Denise Rathbun - 11/26/77 <BR>9-Nancy Fox - 12/8/77 <BR>10-Marine Hedge - 4/27/85 <BR>11-Linda Shawn Casey - 6/29/85 <BR>12-Vicki Wegerle - 9/16/1986 <BR>13-Delores &#39;Dee&#39; Davis 1/18/91 <BR>Dee Davis was the &#39;Final curtain&#39; and for theatrics the porceain type decorative mask was left near the body.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11820-->
<!--Post: 11824--><!--Time: 1111227431-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11824"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bbyrum9@foothill.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 2:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree with most of what you say. But I would feel the opposite about whether he had killed before the Oteros or after 1991. If you look at your list objectively, could you not say that maybe Davis was the last, but could there be  more inside your timeline? Salina in 1993 was just too close to his brother&#39;s home in Falun, maybe one or two after Davis? Could we opine that maybe that darn death penalty had something to do with it? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11824-->
<!--Post: 11833--><!--Time: 1111244312-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11833"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 6:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He could have killed in California as well plus we don&#39;t know the details of his nieces&#39; &#34;accident&#34; in Colorado...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11833-->
